{"name":"Moon Buggy","hex":"#c7bdc1","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"moon buggy","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Alternative letter-case form of Moon buggy."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/moon_buggy"}],"entries":[{"title":"Lunar Roving Vehicle","blocks":[{"text":"The Lunar Roving Vehicle (LRV) is a battery-powered four-wheeled rover used on the Moon in the last three missions of the American Apollo program during 1971 and 1972. It is popularly called the Moon buggy, a play on the term \"dune buggy\"."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ed/Apollo15LunarRover.jpg/330px-Apollo15LunarRover.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lunar_Roving_Vehicle","wikidata":"Q275816"},{"title":"Buggy (automobile)","blocks":[{"text":"Buggy is generally used to refer to any lightweight automobile with off-road capabilities and sparse bodywork. Most are built either as a kit car or from scratch."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/90/Volkswagen_Country_Buggy.jpg/330px-Volkswagen_Country_Buggy.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Buggy_(automobile)","wikidata":"Q4986177"},{"title":"Moon","blocks":[{"text":"The Moon is the only natural satellite of Earth. It orbits Earth in an elliptical path, at a distance that varies over the year, averaging around 378,000 kilometers (235,000 mi). It completes an orbit in relation to Earth and the Sun (synodically) every 29.5 days. The Moon and Earth are bound by gravitational attraction, which is stronger on the sides facing each other. The resulting tidal forces are the main driver of Earth's tides, and have pulled the Moon to always face Earth with the same near side. This tidal locking effectively synchronizes the Moon's rotation period to its orbital period."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e1/FullMoon2010.jpg/330px-FullMoon2010.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Moon","wikidata":"Q405"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b8/Lander_Rover_Apollo_Mission.jpg/500px-Lander_Rover_Apollo_Mission.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b8/Lander_Rover_Apollo_Mission.jpg/500px-Lander_Rover_Apollo_Mission.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"MOLAB, NASA Illustration, 1960","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALander_Rover_Apollo_Mission.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0d/Moon_Buggy_Ap16-KSC-71PC-777.jpg/500px-Moon_Buggy_Ap16-KSC-71PC-777.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0d/Moon_Buggy_Ap16-KSC-71PC-777.jpg/1280px-Moon_Buggy_Ap16-KSC-71PC-777.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0d/Moon_Buggy_Ap16-KSC-71PC-777.jpg/500px-Moon_Buggy_Ap16-KSC-71PC-777.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Apollo 16 astronauts in the 1-g trainer","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMoon_Buggy_Ap16-KSC-71PC-777.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e1/Apollo15LunarRover2.jpg/500px-Apollo15LunarRover2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e1/Apollo15LunarRover2.jpg/1280px-Apollo15LunarRover2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e1/Apollo15LunarRover2.jpg/500px-Apollo15LunarRover